From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0081: a draw that continues the one before keeps its
 color targets

Astro Bot's draws repeat their color targets 98.7 % of the time (same
images and views, same command buffer, no dispatch between; diagnostic
in the garden), and finding a target, touching it and checking its
metadata clears cost 6.5 % of the command thread at every draw. Caching
the found image (an essay, set aside) saved little: the touch and the
metadata checks were the cost. A slot now keeps the target the draw
before found, and a draw takes it again as it is when nothing but
register writes came between the two: the same command buffer, the same
registers (compared field by field), no image registered or unregistered
anywhere (TextureCache::Epoch), no fill or copy (BufferCache::Transfers),
no dispatch nor draw spent on an image operation. The draw before
touched the image in this command buffer and checked its metadata.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
